WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.810
Citadel starts with slash do.

2
00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:07.050
Describe an engineering outcome, and Citadel chooses the smallest operating lane that can carry it.

3
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:14.810
Longer work gains repository state, recovery, coordination, bounded execution, and a concrete next action around Claude Code or Codex.

4
00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.200
The research begins where orchestration ends.

5
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:23.180
A smaller model is not cheaper when it fails, verification forces a retry, or the operation hides cost.

6
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:30.550
Citadel binds the declared route to observed execution, a model-external verdict, separate cost lenses, and a signed receipt.

7
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.200
Failures remain visible.

8
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.590
Six prospective studies tested that contract.

9
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.290
The first was timeout-sensitive.

10
00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:42.310
The second matched baseline completion but used fifteen point seven percent more GPU energy after escalation.

11
00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:46.780
The third preserved artifact and path integrity, yet missed its economic gate.

12
00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.310
Citadel kept all three failures public.

13
00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:55.900
The first Claude-plus-local calibration gave both policies twelve of twelve verified completions and avoided four Claude calls.

14
00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:58.540
But unsupported local attempts forced recovery.

15
00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:05.110
Its twenty-eight point four percent comparison-cost reduction missed the frozen thirty percent gate, so Citadel rejected it.

16
00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:09.900
A separately frozen hybrid v2 used twelve new tasks and a narrower support envelope.

17
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.480
Always-Claude and Citadel again verified twelve of twelve.

18
00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:18.450
Citadel made eight local attempts, recovered once, and reduced Claude calls from twelve to five.

19
00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:25.940
Provider-reported plus locally modeled comparison cost fell from six point four cents to three point nine cents: thirty-eight point seven percent.

20
00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.520
Every frozen gate passed.

21
00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.720
The boundary matters.

22
00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.000
These were author-selected synthetic tasks on one workstation and one model pair.

23
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.210
Claude Code's returned cost is comparison telemetry, not Seth's subscription bill.

24
00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:40.420
Whole-system energy and actual cash remain unknown.

25
00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:52.100
Sentient funding buys the external validity still missing: independently selected production tasks across repositories, agent stacks, models, tools, and hardware, plus a learned operation-value policy.

26
00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:57.650
The public method and every negative result remain available whether broader savings pass or fail.
